+## ISSUE-007 — Machine-access documentation described weekly data as daily
+
+- **Date:** 2026-10-08
+- **Status:** Resolved
+- **Area:** Public AI/data access guide, generated Markdown, and historical-coverage claims.
+- **Symptoms:** The guide stated that public JSON contained daily observations, while the exporter selects `price_weekly` and `split_weekly`. Annual raw-row counts can also exceed distinct fiscal-year labels and should not be advertised as additional years.
+- **Cause:** Documentation described the upstream price frequency rather than the exported frequency; history rows, fiscal labels and elapsed spans require separate definitions.
+- **Solution:** Corrected the guide to weekly observations. Shared advantages copy uses source-derived example counts with distinct year labels, price spans, and per-company endpoints, including zero/negative financial values while excluding missing observations. Legitimate fiscal transitions remain in the original data.
+- **Why this solution:** Accurate, auditable wording communicates the verified benefit without changing financial observations or claiming daily precision or complete annual coverage from endpoints.
+- **Verification:** Exporter reads weekly tables; 31 Node and 4 Python tests pass. The new contract checks a longer non-constituent history, repeated year labels, missing FCF and generated human/AI content. Production/live checks are recorded in VERIFICATION.md.
+- **Follow-up:** Provider-specific access remains open in ISSUE-006. Rebuild coverage copy when the source snapshot changes.
